Small European factories are squeezed by a red clamp: costs enter, prices cannot pass through, and investment is blocked. Mature editorial magazine illustration, sharp metaphor, no text.

Editorial thumbnail for erickilama.com/policy.

Target art direction:
- mature magazine illustration, close to serious policy press rather than startup/AI gloss;
- metaphor must be specific to the article, not a generic chart or globe;
- drawn/painted composition with adult restraint, sharp shapes, controlled texture;
- palette anchored in the site: black undefined, off-white undefined, policy red undefined, restrained blue undefined;
- 16:9 horizontal thumbnail, strong at 200px wide;
- no readable text, no logos, no flags, no real public figures, no childish cartoon style.

Use the attached reference captures only as general visual direction: premium editorial illustration, disciplined composition, mature colour blocking, and abstract press-cover intelligence. Do not copy any exact artwork, layout, headline, logo, or character.
